---
/* Component — PageMainAside
 * The rail beside the page's content column — related links, a table of
 * contents, supporting notes.
 *
 * Renders <aside> so the rail is announced as complementary content. Its
 * presence is also what switches PageMain to the two-track capped row, via
 * PageMain's `:has(> aside)` rule.
 *
 * `span 1 / content-end` places it in the last content track of PageMain's
 * grid: the rail beside the container on desktop, and the single shared track
 * below it — so it stacks under the container — once the row collapses. The
 * grid lines are flow-relative, so the rail sits at the inline end and mirrors
 * under RTL. min-inline-size: 0 lets long content wrap inside the rail rather
 * than widening its track. */
---

<aside>
  <slot />
</aside>

<style>
  aside {
    grid-column: span 1 / content-end;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }
</style>
